The client entrypoint is already at `src/client/init.client.luau`, but the Rojo mapping in `default.project.json` puts it in the wrong place:

```json
"ReplicatedStorage": {
  "Shared": { "$path": "src/shared" },
  "Client": { "$path": "src/client" },   ← this is the problem
  "Packages": { "$path": "Packages" }
},
```

Scripts under ReplicatedStorage never run, so `print("client")` would never execute. A client entrypoint has to be a LocalScript under `StarterPlayer/StarterPlayerScripts` (or `StarterCharacterScripts`, `StarterGui`, etc.), where it runs for each player. Rojo turns `init.client.luau` in a folder into a LocalScript named after that folder, so the file can stay where it is and only the mapping changes:

```json
{
  "name": "arena",
  "tree": {
    "$className": "DataModel",
    "ReplicatedStorage": {
      "Shared": { "$path": "src/shared" },
      "Packages": { "$path": "Packages" }
    },
    "ServerScriptService": { "Server": { "$path": "src/server" } },
    "StarterPlayer": {
      "StarterPlayerScripts": {
        "Client": { "$path": "src/client" }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

This gives you a LocalScript called `Client` in `StarterPlayer/StarterPlayerScripts`. Nothing references `ReplicatedStorage.Client` yet, so removing that mapping shouldn't break anything. Client-only modules can go in other folders under `src/client`, and anything shared with the server belongs in `src/shared`.

I haven't edited the project file, since you asked where it should go. Do you want me to apply this change?

